

### 18.8 Conformal Mapping

\(w\!=\!U\!+\!i\)

\(\Delta\!\!>\!\!0\)

\(w\!=\!{\cal D}\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto the half-plane \(v\!\leq\!0\); if \(|\omega^{\prime}|\!=\!\omega_{\rm z}(g_{\rm z}\!=\!0)\), the isosceles triangle \(0\omega_{\rm z}\) is mapped onto \(u\!\geq\!0\), \(v\!\leq\!0\).

\(w\!=\!{\cal D}^{\prime}\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto the \(w\)-plane less quadrant III; if \(|\omega^{\prime}|\!=\!\omega\), the triangle \(0\omega_{\rm z}\) is mapped onto \(v\!\geq\!0\), \(v\!\geq\!u\).

\(w\!=\!\xi\!\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto the half-plane \(u\!\geq\!0\). If \(a\!\leq\!\!1\),9 (approx.), \(v\!\leq\!0\); otherwise the image extends into quadrant I. For very large \(a\), the image has a large area in quadrant I.

\(w\!=\!\sigma\!\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto quadrant I if a \(<\!\!1.9\) (approx.), onto quadrants I and II if \(1.9\!\leq\!\!a\!<\!3.8\) (approx.). For large \(a\), \(\arg[\sigma\!\left(\omega_{\rm z}\right)]\!\approx\!\frac{\pi^{2}a}{12}\); consequently the image winds around the origin for large \(a\).

Other maps are described in [18.23] arts. 13.7 (square on circle), 13.11 (ring on plane with 2 slits in line) and in [18.24], p. 35 (double half equilateral triangle on half-plane).

\(\Delta\!>\!\!0\)

\(w\!=\!{\cal D}\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto the half-plane \(v\!\leq\!0\); if \(|\omega^{\prime}|\!=\!\omega_{\rm z}(g_{\rm z}\!=\!0)\), the isosceles triangle \(0\omega_{\rm z}\omega^{\prime}\) is mapped onto \(u\!\geq\!0\), \(v\!\leq\!0\).

\(w\!=\!{\cal D}^{\prime}\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto most of the \(w\)-plane less quadrant III; if \(|\omega^{\prime}_{\rm z}|\!=\!\omega_{\rm z}\), the triangle \(0\omega_{\rm z}\omega^{\prime}\) is mapped onto \(v\!\geq\!0\), \(v\!\geq\!u\).

\(w\!=\!\xi\!\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto the half-plane \(u\!\geq\!0\). The image is mostly in quadrant IV for small \(a\), entirely so for (approx.) \(1.3\!\leq\!a\!\leq\!3.8\). For very large \(a\), the image has a large area in quadrant I.

\(w\!=\!\sigma\!\left(z\right)\) maps the Fundamental Rectangle onto quadrant I if \(a\!<\!\!3.8\) (approx.), onto quadrants I and II if \(3.8\!\leq\!a\!<\!7.6\) (approx.). For large \(a\), \(\arg[\sigma\!\left(\omega_{\rm z}\!+\!\frac{\omega^{\prime}_{\rm z}}{2}\right)] \!\approx\!\frac{\pi^{2}a}{24}\); consequently the image winds around the origin for large \(a\).

Other maps are described in [18.23] arts. 13.8 (equilateral triangle on half-plane) and 13.9 (isosceles triangle on half-plane).

